\section{Methodology}
\label{sec:meth}
%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%

\subsection{Overview}
\label{sec:meth-over}
Within-gene synergy networks were used to capture non-linear epistatic effects in the DAISY cohort and summarized through diffusion kernel principal components (kPCs). Between-gene epistasis was detected through a Bayesian interaction analysis of kPC-summarized genes. Gene pairs with evidence of interaction were then included pairwise in an intelligable Random Forest known as Explainable Boost Machine (EBM) at the SNP level to identify SNPs contributing to IA interacting across genes.

\subsection{Data Preparation}
\label{sec:dataprep}
After quality control, 359 DAISY children selected for nested case-control study with a customized Exome array imputed to the TOPMed r2 reference panel were included for analysis of genome-wide epistasis detection.  

